{"id": 13, "ts": 1780476186.321979, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fB\u2019s reliability and stress handling, but I\u2019m concerned we haven\u2019t yet examined the full picture for the other candidates, especially regarding decision quality and crew cooperation\u2014key safety criteria. Candidate\u202fC is noted as 100\u202f% reliable and creates a positive crew atmosphere, which directly addresses operational reliability and cooperation, yet we still lack evidence on how quickly they make decisions under pressure. Candidate\u202fA, while strong in anticipating danger and seeing complex connections, has no documented evidence of consistent reliability or calmness under stress, and they are sometimes resistant to criticism, which could hinder feedback orientation. Candidate\u202fD solves problems extremely well and takes responsibility seriously, but the \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d attitude and hot temper raise red flags for professional communication and teamwork. Given these mixed signals, I remain unconvinced that Candidate\u202fB\u2019s communication concerns are less severe than the potential issues with the others. I therefore keep my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fC, because their proven reliability and crew\u2011positive demeanor outweigh the unverified strengths of the other applicants."}
